[
    {
        "content": "<p>The <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Order/GroupWithZero/Unbundled/Defs.html\">module docstring of <code>Mathlib.Algebra.Order.GroupWithZero.Unbundled.Defs</code></a> mentions <code>OrderedSemiring</code>/<code>StrictOrderedSemiring</code>/<code>OrderedAddCommMonoid</code>/<code>LinearOrderedField</code>, and the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Order/GroupWithZero/Unbundled/Defs.html#PosMulReflectLT\">docstrings</a> of the classes defined there recommend the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"txt\"><pre><span></span><code>You should usually not use this very granular typeclass directly,\nbut rather a typeclass like `OrderedSemiring`/`StrictOrderedSemiring`/`LinearOrderedSemiring`.\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Should these old typeclasses be replaced according to the table in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/20676\">#20676</a>, or is it not so simple?<br>\nIs the advice to not use classes such as <code>PosMulMono</code> itself old and can be removed?</p>\n<p>cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"455791\">@Yuyang Zhao</span> as the authors of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/8841\">#8841</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/20676\">#20676</a> respectively</p>\n<p>(also if anyone opens a PR then while we're at it there's a Zulip link in the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Order/GroupWithZero/Unbundled/Defs.html#Notation\">notation section</a> that isn't picked up by doc-gen, so should probably be wrapped with angle brackets)</p>",
        "id": 584375257,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1775718287
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this documentation should probably be updated</p>",
        "id": 584379316,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1775719459
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>we should still be using the non-granular typeclasses I think</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">You</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">should</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">usually</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">very</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">granular</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">typeclass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">directly</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rather</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">typeclass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">like</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`IsOrderedRing</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">or</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`IsStrictOrderedRing</span><span class=\"bp\">`.</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 584399891,
